WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.880
Hi, Mystery Recapped here. Today I am going&nbsp;
to explain an American fantasy drama film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:16.160
called “Wendy.” Spoilers ahead!&nbsp;
Watch out and take care!
&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.440
The movie starts in Darling’s diner owned&nbsp;
by a middle-aged woman named Angela Darling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:26.560
She has three kids, two twin sons, James&nbsp;
and Douglas, and a younger daughter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:31.840
Wendy. Their dinner lies right by a railroad&nbsp;
in the rural South and is always filled with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:37.600
people. It is a happy and lively place where&nbsp;
everybody loves little Wendy. One day, a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:43.040
guy named Thomas Marshall is in the diner enjoying&nbsp;
a meal for his seventh birthday. His grandmother
&nbsp;

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.160
jokes that he will be a cleaner at the diner&nbsp;
when he grows up. Thomas retaliates; he wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.840
be a pirate but the seniors just laugh at him.&nbsp;
Overwhelmed with emotions, he walks outside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:58.720
when no one is watching. Little Wendy, who is&nbsp;
some years younger than Thomas, crawls towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:03.840
the window and watches as he gets on a moving&nbsp;
train. There seems to be another child on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:09.600
train with him, whose face isn’t clearly seen.
Time passes and Wendy gets older but she never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.120
forgets what she saw that day. She becomes more&nbsp;
imaginative with time and often writes her own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:20.560
bedtime stories about adventures. At only nine&nbsp;
years old, she has a thirst for adventures and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:26.480
willing to take risks for a rush of adrenaline. As&nbsp;
Wendy helps her mother and brothers at the diner&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.280
we see a notice on a board that says Thomas&nbsp;
disappeared at the age of seven and has never been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:36.400
found, along with another thirteen-year-old boy,&nbsp;
indicating that children go missing frequently in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:42.640
the town. Wendy is calm and composed in contrast&nbsp;
to her brothers who are always dancing, singing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.840
and making noise. The four of them are&nbsp;
a happy family nonetheless. One night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:53.200
on the boy’s demand, their mother tells them a&nbsp;
bedtime story about her life. She claims that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:58.080
was wild when she was younger and had dreams and&nbsp;
aspirations that people would make fun of her for.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:04.560
She once hitchhiked to California and stole&nbsp;
cars on her way. Wendy is fascinated and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.680
asks her what her dreams are now. Angela replies&nbsp;
that she wants to take care of her children.
&nbsp;

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.880
She adds, as people get older and things&nbsp;
change, their dreams also change. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.600
makes Wendy sad because she never wants to give&nbsp;
up her dream of going on several adventures and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.840
she doesn’t want to get old either. The following&nbsp;
day after school, the kids go to a canal to fish.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:31.120
James and Douglas are busy when Wendy runs towards&nbsp;
the railway tracks. She sees a train and chases&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:37.040
behind it hoping to board it as Thomas did years&nbsp;
ago. But she falls in the way and misses it. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:42.160
returning home, she remembers her brother’s words;&nbsp;
Your life will go by and nothing will ever happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.800 --> 00:02:47.680
At night, everyone is asleep but Wendy keeps&nbsp;
herself busy by making up stories about stars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:53.120
Suddenly, a mysterious red light passes through&nbsp;
the window and the sound of a train approaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.000
is heard. She looks outside the window and sees&nbsp;
a boy playing and running on top of a moving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.520
train. It is the same little boy named Peter,&nbsp;
who was with Thomas when he disappeared. 
&nbsp;

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.360
Wendy wakes her brothers up and climbs&nbsp;
out of the window to take a closer look.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:11.120
The boys follow her behind but cannot&nbsp;
stop her before she jumps on the train.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:17.440
They, too, get on board following their sister.&nbsp;
Wendy spreads her arms feeling free for the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:22.800
time. Then, they are approached by a laughing&nbsp;
Peter. The guys ask him what their stop is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:28.080
but Peter replies that there are no stops because&nbsp;
this is an adventure. In the morning, Peter tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:33.760
Wendy that the world has no end; it goes on and&nbsp;
on forever past the restaurants and the houses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:41.120
When they reach above a river, Peter asks them to&nbsp;
line up on the edge of the train. The kids do it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:46.720
without asking any questions and yell in fear when&nbsp;
they are pushed into the river by him. Peter jumps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:51.520
behind them and introduces them to a kid on a&nbsp;
boat. All of them get on the boat and sail to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:57.200
the sea, eventually reaching a volcanic tropical&nbsp;
island. A fish-like creature from the sea makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.720
a noise that Peter claims is the mother welcoming&nbsp;
them. Seeing the magical island, Wendy remembers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.680
the voice in her head that used to ask her to&nbsp;
sneak into the night. She figures that the noise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:13.120
has been coming from the island all along. 
An active volcano is shooting out smoke in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:18.160
air, indicating the magical charge of the place.&nbsp;
Peter runs into the woods with his friend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.640
making the siblings follow them. On their&nbsp;
way, they are terrorized by smoke coming out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:28.320
of the ground. A while later, they meet a guy&nbsp;
their age singing a melody to the big volcano.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:33.520
Wendy joins him out of nowhere. Peter approaches&nbsp;
them and says that their singing was hopeless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:39.040
He meditates and performs some hand gestures of&nbsp;
his own, triggering the volcano. The others run&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.800
away in fear and excitement. Suddenly, a little&nbsp;
boy comes running their way, who Wendy recognizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.920
as Thomas. Although he was older than her when&nbsp;
he ran away, he doesn’t seem to have aged a day.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.920
Upon inquiry, Thomas claims that he is a&nbsp;
Blackbeard and runs away. At night, the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.920 --> 00:05:01.840
kids play and laugh around the confused Darling&nbsp;
siblings. Eventually, they join the others and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.840 --> 00:05:06.560
start singing the same melody from earlier. 
When they wake up the next morning, Peter is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:12.160
looking at the sea, claiming that he is talking&nbsp;
to the mother. Later, he and Wendy jump into a pit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:17.200
on the ground and reach a canal. Peter takes&nbsp;
her into the sea and shows her the mother who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:22.320
turns out to be the island’s spirit in the form&nbsp;
of a massive fish that spreads a golden glow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:27.520
wherever it goes. Peter explains that when the&nbsp;
first child laughed, for the first time, the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:32.720
mother rose up to the surface from the center of&nbsp;
the earth to watch over them. She preserves their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.760
childhood so they can go on any adventure and&nbsp;
do whatever they want for as long as they like.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:42.960
However, the magic only works if you maintain&nbsp;
faith in the mother. If someone stops believing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:47.760
in her, they will age at an exponential&nbsp;
rate and turn old. For the next few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:53.840
life is like a movie for the children. They play,&nbsp;
dance, sing and laugh from day to night without&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:58.880
any care. Douglas and James completely forget&nbsp;
about their mother back home but Wendy thinks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:03.920
herself that she is just extending her visit and&nbsp;
will return home once she is done having fun. 
&nbsp;

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:10.240
One day, Wendy wakes up to see an elderly man&nbsp;
wandering close by. When she greets him, he runs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.240 --> 00:06:15.280
off into a barren side of the island. The children&nbsp;
explain his name is Buzzo, a former member of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:20.560
their group who lost faith in Mother when he lost&nbsp;
his best friend, and so aged into an old man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:26.240
After that, they find a capsized boat called the&nbsp;
Mañana in the sea. The Darling siblings swim to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:31.680
the boat to inspect it. Douglas is skeptical about&nbsp;
swimming into the compartments of the ship but he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:37.200
agrees when James calls him a coward. The three&nbsp;
dive into the compartment but only James and Wendy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:42.880
emerge from the other side. Worried for Douglas,&nbsp;
they dive back inside but are unable to find him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.760
The other kids also help them look but are&nbsp;
unsuccessful. Eventually, they drag the brother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:53.760
and the sister out of water assuring them that&nbsp;
Douglas must be fine. Losing his twin, affects&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:59.680
James the most. When he wakes up the next day, his&nbsp;
hand has wrinkled and turned old. Wendy realizes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.240
that James has lost faith in the mother and he&nbsp;
asks her to keep it a secret from the others. 
&nbsp;

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:10.320
However, Peter soon finds out about it. James&nbsp;
tries to snatch Peter’s sword to cut his old arm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:15.920
off to try to stop the aging process. Peter&nbsp;
volunteers to do it himself and cut his arm.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:20.880
Wendy runs to her brother who falls to the ground&nbsp;
in pain. She angrily asks everyone to get away&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:26.640
from them and takes James with her in search of an&nbsp;
actual adult. They come across Buzzo who agrees to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.760
help them. He puts James on a donkey and takes&nbsp;
the two to the old people’s quarter. It is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:36.480
place where all the children who have turned into&nbsp;
old people live. Everyone there is catching and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:42.000
killing fishes which confuses Wendy. She inquires&nbsp;
what they are doing to find out that eating the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:46.000
mother will give old people their childhood&nbsp;
back, so they are trying to catch her. 
&nbsp;

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:52.320
James’s arm is now tied in a cloth and has stopped&nbsp;
bleeding. To rest, he and Wendy go to an abandoned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:57.920
diner with the other old people. Silence prevails&nbsp;
in the room until Wendy asks everyone to bring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.920 --> 00:08:03.520
their childhood spirits back even if they are&nbsp;
old. She dances, urging the others to do the same.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:09.280
Eventually, all of them get together and dance&nbsp;
Except for James, who is still very depressed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:14.240
He runs out in frustration as Wendy follows him&nbsp;
behind. James goes to the fishing zone and gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:19.280
the nets ready. The other old people see this and&nbsp;
decide to make him their leader because he knows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:24.080
how to fish. James comes out with another plan&nbsp;
to capture the mother. He suggests they abduct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:28.880
the children which will make the mother come to&nbsp;
them herself. Wendy retaliates against the idea&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.880 --> 00:08:34.080
but the others like it. They start to prepare to&nbsp;
kidnap the kids while Wendy runs back to the woods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:39.360
to alert them. But the adults get there before&nbsp;
her and kidnap all the children. The only one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.360 --> 00:08:44.800
that could hide and save himself is Peter. Wendy&nbsp;
joins him and the two watch the adults repair the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:49.920
boat Mañana and board the kids on it. 
Wendy notices a man with only one arm&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:55.760
bending a hook. It turns out that the man is&nbsp;
James who has grown into an adult. After they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.760 --> 00:09:00.160
sail away with the boat, Peter urges Wendy&nbsp;
to come with him and save their friends.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:05.520
They jump into the ocean and end up in the canal&nbsp;
again. There, Peter tells Wendy about his family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:11.440
back home. Wendy wanders off to the other side&nbsp;
of the canal to find Douglas alive and well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:16.800
The two reunite and set off to look for their&nbsp;
friends on a rowboat. Seeing no one on the deck,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:21.520
the three of them climb up the boat and try to&nbsp;
untie the children, but the adults catch them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:26.720
and bring them to their leader, James. He has&nbsp;
now turned fully old and has a hook in the place&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.240
of his missing arm. James and Douglas are both&nbsp;
surprised to see each other. James is mad at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:38.000
him for staying young while he turned old. While&nbsp;
Douglas refuses to believe James is his brother.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:42.960
Suddenly, the sound of the mother is heard. 
The adults all prepare to hunt her while the kids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:47.840
beg them to stop. They free themselves and jump&nbsp;
into the water to get the mother out of the net&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:53.600
but are too late as James strikes her with a&nbsp;
harpoon and injures her gravely. The golden glow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:58.480
from the mother’s body dissociates and drops&nbsp;
to the bottom of the ocean. James manages to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.480 --> 00:10:04.320
get a piece of flesh from the mother’s body but&nbsp;
refuses to eat it at last. Peter cries in vain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:09.440
about losing the mother and Wendy comforts him&nbsp;
by hugging him. He is worried that he will now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:15.760
get old and die. Now, even makes the olds feel bad&nbsp;
for the kid. Wendy assures all of them that their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:21.040
story is great and the bigger they get, the more&nbsp;
stories they can form. They can get married and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:26.080
have children who will have stories of their own.&nbsp;
Hence, they should not be disheartened. She then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:31.120
gets them to all start singing the melody again.&nbsp;
As their singing grows louder, Peter becomes more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:37.120
inspired, and the volcano erupts once more. Wendy&nbsp;
and Douglas decide it is time for them to go home.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:42.080
Knowing that he cannot go home, James&nbsp;
says his last goodbye to his twin.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:47.920
He then changes his name to Captain Hook and&nbsp;
stays to play with Peter as his new “enemy”,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:52.640
thereby allowing him to live out the rest&nbsp;
of his days with the spirit of a child.
&nbsp;

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:57.840
In the ending monologue, Wendy says that she,&nbsp;
Douglas, and the other children have returned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.840 --> 00:11:03.600
home to their own families. They have many&nbsp;
adventures as they grow older. They dance and sing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:09.200
and have fun even as adults. Many years later,&nbsp;
Wendy is now a mother with her own daughter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:18.480
She tells the story of Peter and the island to her&nbsp;
as a bedtime story. At night, while Wendy sleeps,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:23.760
her daughter hops on the train with Peter. Wendy&nbsp;
runs after, but she cannot catch up to them. She&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:29.120
then watches them get away with a smile on her&nbsp;
face, knowing that her daughter is in good hands&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:37.520
and is ready for an adventure of her own.
